  "agent": {
    "note": "**Canvas perf: the cursor track no longer explodes the overlay stack.** Same walk you've approved — verify the orange ring still leads the parse correctly; only how it's drawn changed.\n\n**The bottleneck was the cursor.** The canvas composited **one masked full-panel tile per step** (one orange ring = one overlay layer), so step count drove overlay DEPTH — the dominant render cost (the frame threads through every layer, super-linear, and masks silently drop past ~25). 4×4 ≈ 21 steps → a ~21-deep masked-overlay stack; 8×8 ≈ 154 → the 30-min render.\n\n**Your fix, exactly:** rects, no mask, orange, enable-gated. The whole cursor track is now **ONE `lavfi` source** — a flat chain of ffmpeg `drawbox` ops, one per step, each gated to its window. `drawbox` draws all four edges natively (no input, no mask, native thickness), so the track is a **single overlay layer regardless of step count**. Depth O(steps) → O(1).\n\n**Measured (perf sidecar, 4×4):**\n\n| | canvas self | total | bottleneck |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| before | **37.9s** (61%) | 62.5s | canvas |\n| after | **9.0s** (27%) | 33.3s | moved → dsl-string |\n\nCanvas −76%, total −47%, and the bottleneck moved *off* the canvas. Verified the orange ring still renders + toggles (≈200 px ring present at t=1.5s and t=4.0s).\n\n*(14 canvas tests green. Splits stay inline-mask — they're dashed, drawbox can't dash, and they're cheap/bounded. Learning written up at `.ai/candidates/2026-06-29-drawbox-track-collapse.md`.)*",
    "question": "Does the geometry cursor still read correctly on this 4×4 — crisp orange ring at the live X/Y/W/H bounds, one lit at a time, leading the parse exactly as before? If yes, the canvas collapse is approved and the next bottleneck is **dsl-string** (now 45%). If the ring looks off (thickness, inset, color, timing), tell me what's wrong.",
    "context": {
      "category": {
        "kind": "other",
        "label": "canvas-perf-drawbox"
      },
      "intent": {
        "action": "propose",
        "summary": "Collapse the O(steps) masked-ring cursor overlays into ONE lavfi drawbox track (depth O(steps)→O(1)); canvas self-time −76% on 4×4, bottleneck moves off canvas."
      },
      "relation": {
        "kind": "refines",
        "target": "018"
      }
    }
  }
